{"page": 1, "text": "Visible text of EX-99.1_2026-10-21_moh3q26_er.htm, sha256 f02332bbf441a77762637927e38598a78fe29ff2bf7645599d0f55d6d5a9be2e.\nEX-99.1 2 moh3q26_er.htm EX-99.1 News Release Investor Contact: Jeffrey Geyer, Jeffrey.Geyer@molinahealthcare.com, 305-317-3012 Media Contact: Caroline Zubieta, Caroline.Zubieta@molinahealthcare.com, 562-542-1845\nMolina Healthcare Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results Reaffirms Full Year 2026 Earnings Guidance Long Beach, Calif., October 21, 2026 \u2013 Molina Healthcare, Inc. (NYSE: MOH) (the \u201cCompany\u201d) today reported third quarter 2026 GAAP income per diluted share of $0.73 and adjusted income per diluted share of $0.89. Financial results are summarized below:\nThree months ended Nine months ended\nSeptember 30, September 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\n(In millions, except per-share results)\nPremium Revenue $10,457 $10,841 $30,873 $32,337\nTotal Revenue $11,082 $11,477 $32,752 $34,051\nGAAP:\nNet Income $38 $79 $112 $632\nEPS \u2013 Diluted $0.73 $1.51 $2.19 $11.79\nMedical Care Ratio (MCR) 92.9 % 92.6 % 92.1 % 90.8 %\nG&A Ratio 6.4 % 6.4 % 6.8 % 6.5 %\nPre-tax Margin 0.5 % 0.8 % 0.5 % 2.4 %\nAdjusted:\nNet Income $46 $97 $243 $724\nEPS \u2013 Diluted $0.89 $1.84 $4.74 $13.49\nG&A Ratio 6.3 % 6.3 % 6.6 % 6.4 %\nPre-tax Margin 0.6 % 1.0 % 1.1 % 2.7 %\nSee the Reconciliation of Unaudited Non-GAAP Financial Measures at the end of this release.\nQuarter Highlights \u2022As of September 30, 2026, the Company served approximately 4.9 million members. \u2022Premium revenue was approximately $10.5 billion for the third quarter of 2026. \u2022Third quarter 2026 GAAP income per diluted share was $0.73 and adjusted income per diluted share was $0.89. \u2022The Company reaffirmed its full year 2026 guidance of expected premium revenue of approximately $42 billion and adjusted earnings of at least $5.25 per diluted share.\n\u201cWe are pleased with our third quarter results in this challenging environment and reaffirm our full year guidance,\u201d said Joseph Zubretsky, President and Chief Executive Officer. \u201cWith the apparent plateauing of medical cost trend, which remains at elevated levels, and the strength of recent rate updates for 2027, we believe we are likely observing the beginning of the turn in Medicaid margins.\u201d\n-MORE- Molina Healthcare, Inc. Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results Page 2 October 21, 2026 Premium Revenue Premium revenue was approximately $10.5 billion for the third quarter of 2026, a decrease of 4% year over year. The lower premium revenue reflects the impact of lower membership in Medicaid and Marketplace, partially offset by rate updates.\nNet Income GAAP net income for the third quarter of 2026 was $38 million, or $0.73 per diluted share, a decrease of 52% year over year. Adjusted net income for the third quarter of 2026 was $46 million, or $0.89 per diluted share, a decrease of 53% year over year. The decrease is attributed mainly to a higher consolidated MCR.\n"}
{"page": 2, "text": "Medical Care Ratio (MCR) \u2022The consolidated MCR for the third quarter of 2026 was 92.9%. \u2022The Medicaid MCR for the third quarter of 2026 was 93.0% and in line with the Company\u2019s expectations, reflecting rate updates and stable medical cost trend. \u2022The Medicare MCR for the third quarter of 2026 was 93.0% and in line with the Company\u2019s expectations, reflecting stable medical cost trend. \u2022The Marketplace MCR for the third quarter of 2026 was 92.5% and in line with normal seasonality and the Company\u2019s expectations.\nGeneral and Administrative Expense Ratio The G&A ratio and the adjusted G&A ratio for the third quarter of 2026 were 6.4% and 6.3%, respectively, reflecting continued operating discipline.\nBalance Sheet Cash and investments at the parent company were approximately $608 million as of September 30, 2026, compared to $223 million as of December 31, 2025. Days in claims payable at September 30, 2026, was 44, consistent with June 30, 2026.\nCash Flow Operating cash flow for the nine months ended September 30, 2026, was $629 million, compared to an outflow of $237 million for the nine months ended September 30, 2025. The increase compared to the prior year was driven mainly by lower government receivable and payable settlements in 2026.\n2026 Guidance Premium revenue guidance for the full year is unchanged at approximately $42 billion. The Company expects its full year 2026 GAAP earnings to be at least $2.38 per diluted share and reaffirmed its full year 2026 adjusted earnings of at least $5.25 per diluted share. Guidance metrics across all segments are also reaffirmed. Full year earnings guidance includes a loss of $1.50 per share due to the implementation of the new Florida Medicaid contract in the fourth quarter of 2026 and a loss of $1.00 per share due to performance of the traditional MAPD product, which the Company previously announced it will exit for 2027.\n-MORE- Molina Healthcare, Inc. Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results Page 3 October 21, 2026 Conference Call Management will host a conference call and webcast to discuss Molina Healthcare\u2019s third quarter ended September 30, 2026 results, at 8:00 a.m. Eastern Time on Thursday, October 22, 2026. The number to call for the interactive teleconference is (877) 883-0383 and the confirmation number is 6534841. A telephonic replay of the conference call will be available through Thursday, October 29, 2026, by dialing (855) 669-9658 and entering confirmation number 4361465. A live audio broadcast of this conference call will be available on Molina Healthcare\u2019s investor relations website, investors.molinahealthcare.com. A 30-day online replay will be available approximately an hour following the conclusion of the live broadcast.\n"}
{"page": 3, "text": "About Molina Healthcare Molina Healthcare, Inc., a FORTUNE 500 company, provides managed healthcare services under the Medicaid and Medicare programs and through the state insurance marketplaces. For more information about Molina Healthcare, please visit molinahealthcare.com.\n"}
